# Sensitive paths for shipping-work's doc-check.sh, Step 1.5 (#488).
#
# Files whose existence, names or structure the docs inventory: a branch that
# touches one of these probably owes a doc section an edit. One path per line,
# blank lines and #-comments ignored, same grammar as .skills/import-targets.
# Entries match whole path SEGMENTS at any depth, so `scripts/` also reaches
# `tests/scripts/` — over-matching is the cheap failure for a spot-check that
# exits 1 and asks a human to look (gregoryfoster/skills#252).
#
# This file REPLACES the skill's built-in defaults rather than extending them.
# Five of those twelve describe a layout this service does not have:
# CHANGELOG.md, alembic/versions/ (schema is src/core/schema.sql plus
# reconciliation DO blocks), deploy/ (infra/), src/models/ (no ORM package)
# and .env.example (/etc/power-map/.env plus a gitignored .env).
#
# Guarded by tests/test_doc_sensitive_paths.py: every entry must match a
# tracked file, and each documented tree must stay covered.
# Deliberately absent: docs/ (a doc edit is not a signal to check the docs) and
# tests/ (TDD means every branch touches it, so it would make the gate constant).

# Agent-context surface and orientation
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
README.md

# Dependency and build manifests — pyproject/package.json are a version-sync pair
pyproject.toml
package.json
uv.lock
package-lock.json

# The domain contract, inventoried by docs/SCHEMA*.md
schema.sql

# Application code the docs describe route by route and panel by panel
src/api/
src/core/
src/templates/
src/static/

# Operations: systemd units, terraform, and the operational scripts
infra/
scripts/

# Agent tooling docs/SKILLS.md and docs/SOCRATICODE.md inventory by name
.claude/hooks/
.claude/skills/
.claude/settings.json
skills/
.gitmodules
.socraticodecontextartifacts.json
